# The demo site is its own standalone repo (preserved separately) — never
# absorb it into this monorepo. Still Demo-MyKurda on disk and in its own
# history: the rebrand renamed the product, not a folder somebody else owns,
# and an ignore rule that does not match the directory is no ignore rule.
# See Demo-MyKurda/README.md.
/Demo-MyKurda/

# Old drop folders for cosmetic art. The shop's backgrounds and icons are drawn by
# scripts/generate-cosmetic-art.mjs and committed under web/public/cosmetics, with
# the catalogue in api/content/cosmetics.json; these stay ignored so nothing left
# in one can be swept into a commit.
/default-avatars/
/premium-icons/
/hevalo-background/
/mykurda-background/

# Where source artwork is dropped for conversion: sticker PNGs, the empty-state
# drawings, the avatars and the logo. What ships is generated from these —
# sized WebPs under web/public/stickers, the four PNGs under mobile/assets/empty,
# and everything scripts/generate-brand-assets.mjs writes.
# Ignored so a `git add -A` cannot sweep multi-megabyte originals into a commit.
/stickers/
/empty/
/Profiles/
/Logo/
/Logos/
/kurdistan_filter.png
__pycache__/
